  "lines": [
   {"id": "hook",  "text": "When you get paid, who gets paid first?"},
   {"id": "most",  "text": "For most people, it's everyone else. Rent, bills, shopping. Then they save whatever is left, if anything."},
   {"id": "flip",  "text": "Rich Dad Poor Dad flips the order. Pay yourself first."},
   {"id": "asset", "text": "Before the bills, a slice of every paycheck goes into your asset column. Things that bring money in."},
   {"id": "rule",  "text": "Kiyosaki says this takes self-discipline. And when money is tight, don't dip into it. Use the pressure to find new ways to earn."},
   {"id": "ask",   "text": "So ask yourself: when your next paycheck lands, who gets paid first?"},
   {"id": "cta",   "text": "Follow Lobe for one book lesson every day."}
